__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.idea/

# Obsidian vault config is local-only: personal editor prefs (app.json),
# per-session UI state (workspace.json), and large third-party plugin/theme
# binaries (~2.4 MB — like node_modules). The study content itself (notes,
# flashcards, Glossary, MOC) is plain markdown and stays tracked.
# On a fresh clone, re-enable the Spaced Repetition plugin in Obsidian.
**/.obsidian/

# NOTE: vaults/ccaf/Weak Areas.md ships with a template ("no misses logged
# yet") that IS tracked. /study then appends a per-user "Miss log" locally —
# personal study history, not shareable course content. Because .gitignore
# can't hide further edits to an already-tracked file, that file is marked
# `git update-index --skip-worktree` instead: git keeps the checked-in
# template for other downloaders but never diffs or commits this machine's
# local miss log. Run `git update-index --no-skip-worktree` on it first if
# you ever need to actually commit a change to the template itself.

# Build/session state: run.json, inventory.json, domain/eval logs, and the
# hook-appended *.jsonl files. This is local machine state (absolute source
# paths under the user's home directory, per-session transcript paths,
# timestamps of individual work sessions) — not portable course content, and
# not something to publish for other downloaders. SOURCE_INVENTORY.md and
# COVERAGE_GAPS.md (generated from this state with paths rendered relative to
# `~`) stay tracked as the shareable summary.
.claude/state/*/*.json
.claude/state/*/*.jsonl
!.claude/state/*/.gitkeep
